    "VISUAL_NAME": "Stacked Column",
    "SCHEMA_NAME": "FAM_DEPRECIATION_COMPARISON_CA_IT",
    "SCHEMA_DESCR": "Depreciation Comparison - Companies Act vs Income Tax. SEVERE ASSUMPTION: no depreciation-postings/ledger table exists for either Companies Act or Income Tax (no MONTHLY_DEPRECIATION_AMOUNT / DEPRECIATION_AMOUNT table in this project's design), and FAM_ASSET_REGISTER carries no CATEGORY_CODE, INCOME_TAX_BLOCK_CODE or cost basis to link individual assets to either rate master. A true 'depreciation amount by month/year and method' chart as specified in the FRS cannot be computed from the given schema. This visual is therefore NOT an amount comparison but a STATUTORY RATE comparison built entirely from real master data (FAM_DEP_RATE_CA_MASTER, FAM_DEP_RATE_IT_MASTER): for each Companies Act category, the effective annual SLM/WDV rate implied by (100-RESIDUAL_VALUE_PCT)/USEFUL_LIFE_YEARS (SLM) or 1-(RESIDUAL_VALUE_PCT/100)^(1/USEFUL_LIFE_YEARS) (WDV); for each Income Tax block, its prescribed RATE_PCT directly - both taken as the latest rate version with EFFECTIVE_FROM_DATE <= the As On Date filter. Because Companies Act categories and Income Tax blocks are different keyspaces with no mapping table between them in this schema, the bars do NOT represent the SAME underlying asset group side-by-side - they show the two acts' prescribed rate schedules independently, stacked by method on one axis. Replace with a real per-asset/per-category depreciation ledger (with CATEGORY_CODE/BLOCK_CODE link and cost basis) once such a table is added to the schema. The dashboard's BRANCH_CODE filter does not apply here since rate masters carry no branch dimension.",
    "SCHEMA_TYPE": "S",
    "OUTPUT_TYPE": "JSON",
    "DATABASE_TYPE": "1",
    "DATABASE_DETAIL": { "DATABASE_NAME": "PostgreSQL", "TYPE": 1 }
